# SABOTAGE: issue #11 — `samen_anthropic` stops recognising Anthropic's "prompt is too long"
# rejection (a 400 `invalid_request_error`), so an input that exceeds the context window
# comes back as a generic `{:anthropic_error, 400, ...}`, the chokepoint normalizes it to
# `{:provider_error, _}`, and ADR-048 §6 Level 2 recovery never fires on the one real
# adapter. The state before #11's follow-up.
#
# Flips the prompt-too-long test. The narrow-classifier control (any OTHER invalid request
# stays a bounded provider error) stays green.
# APP: samen_anthropic
# TEST_FILES: test/provider_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a 400 'prompt is too long' is a :context_overflow — nothing was spent, so no usage
diff --git a/samen_anthropic/lib/samen_anthropic/provider.ex b/samen_anthropic/lib/samen_anthropic/provider.ex
index bdbbb81..3feff57 100644
--- a/samen_anthropic/lib/samen_anthropic/provider.ex
+++ b/samen_anthropic/lib/samen_anthropic/provider.ex
@@ -172,7 +172,8 @@ defmodule SamenAnthropic.Provider do
   end
 
   defp prompt_too_long?(message),
-    do: message |> String.downcase() |> String.contains?("prompt is too long")
+    # SABOTAGE (#11): the classifier never recognises the overflow message.
+    do: message |> String.downcase() |> String.contains?("prompt is too short")
 
   # All three input fields count toward the window (see the moduledoc).
   defp normalize_usage(usage) when is_map(usage) do
